This product is a derivative work of pagecat/vowifi_gateway
(https://github.com/pagecat/vowifi_gateway, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 pagecat),
which contributes the VoWiFi engine and the overall control-plane, engine and WebUI
architecture. MDD Sim Gateway adds 4G cellular data and SMS, per-country network egress
routing, unified device management and automatic provisioning, failover and a test suite.
It also includes modified code derived from fasferraz/SWu-IKEv2 and integration work
based on phcoder/asterisk-docker, and it builds, downloads, links to, or communicates
with the independent components listed in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.

The legacy engine image builds sysmocom's Asterisk (GPL-2.0-only) and pjproject
(GPL-2.0-or-later, used there under GPL-2.0) from pinned commits.
The cellular modem's SIM slots are served by the virtual PC/SC driver from
frankmorgner/vsmartcard (GPL-3.0), installed from the distribution's vsmartcard-vpcd package.
